# A board about how the client draws piles of like lands, handed over with Bot1 holding priority in its own main
# phase. Five Forests, two of them spent: the client draws the three untapped ones as one pile and the two tapped
# ones as another, which is what a pile is for — five Forests are one fact about the turn and not five cards to read.
#
# Clicking one of the untapped ones taps it for mana, which takes a card out of one pile and puts it into the other
# and slides everything left in the tapped pile along a step. That is the movement this position exists to picture:
#
# then click an untapped Forest, and another before the first one's cards have landed, which is how a player tapping
# lands makes them.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T9 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[Handover Bot1.Pass]

[Expect]
Turn = 9
Step = Main1
ActivePlayer = Bot1
PriorityPlayer = Bot1
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
# Two spent and three still to spend, which is the two piles.
Bot1.Mana = {G}{G}
